hangeling-kids?p=1087525#post1087525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How would that be different than Lenore's situation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would be a child adopted by both the King and Queen. As oppose to Lenore who is only David's heir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T03:40:04-07:00","id":1087605,"title":"","content":"Despite the fact, that Sidhe act like real life nobility their founding history shows, that they were more like meritocratic clubs, who overtime adopted lifestyles and culture of fantasy medieval knights &amp; nobility.<br /> <br /> So, to adopt a heir to cover that particular inconsistency and the fact, that they are just a mockup aristocracy seems to be a fair game. <br /> <br /> Also, Dreaming supports that kind of farce, so consider, that rules are subject to bend - when plot demands they might have a Changeling child, who's also a Sidhe unless something else would be more dramatic. Also, Dreaming might retcon some appropriate prophesy to make everything look, like it's all going according to plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-04-2017, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"rea